From 5bb0e2e2c26b67a9081ca99b7c6b1005b225a7ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dborin <james.dborin@doubleword.ai>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:06:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MoE: MOE_SCALE_E8M0 stores GMM expert block scales as uint8
 exponents (exact)

With MOE_SCALE_E8M0=1 (default off; supersedes MOE_SCALE_BF16, which
becomes the fallback) the f32 fp4 block-32 requant scales are stored as
their uint8 f32 biased-exponent codes (code 0 = +0.0 for zero-padded
blocks) when that is lossless (positive normal powers of two or +0,
checked per tensor at load), in XLA's default unpadded layout.
gmm_wrapper rebuilds the exact f32 scales (shift + bitcast) before
gmm_v2, so the kernel input is bit-identical. Saves ~3.0 GiB/chip at TP8
vs f32 (1.0 GiB vs bf16) for one layer's f32 scale copy per gmm call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQhK9cavqLsEnxm6YHREB3
