-    bf16 scales in XLA's default layout, which moves the unit dim major and
-    stores them unpadded (a forced (0,1,2,3) layout tiles the unit dim to 2
-    rows and saves nothing). Cost: one layer's f32 scale copy per gmm call.
+    """MOE_SCALE_E8M0 / MOE_SCALE_BF16: compact GMM expert block scale storage.
+
+    MOE_SCALE_E8M0 stores each scale as its uint8 f32-exponent code (see
+    quantization/e8m0_scale.py; supersedes bf16), MOE_SCALE_BF16 as bf16. The
+    scales are only stored compactly: gmm_wrapper rebuilds the f32 scales right
+    before gmm_v2, so the kernel sees exactly the f32 values it sees today and
+    results are bit-identical. A layer's scale is converted only if the
+    encoding is lossless (checked per tensor; fp4 block-32 requant scales are
+    positive powers of two, so all of them are); otherwise it falls back to
+    bf16 (if enabled and lossless) and then to f32. shard_moe_weights keeps
